--- stdout ---
Static code analysis and command workflow coach

Usage: omnicoach [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  code     Inspect source files and directories
  command  Validate an intercepted shell command string
  graph    [ALPHA — experimental, under active investigation & design; format may change at any
           time] Generate a multi-level abstraction graph for files or directories
  hook     Handle agent lifecycle hook events (`PreToolUse`, `PreInvocation`) from stdin
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format for diagnostics

          Possible values:
          - plain: Human-readable text
          - json:  Pretty-printed JSON array
          
          [default: plain]

      --diff
          Run linter only on files/lines changed in VCS

      --diff-rev <DIFF_REV>
          Run linter comparing against a custom revision/commit (implies --diff)

      --config <PATH>
          Path to the configuration file (overrides `.omnicoach.toml` discovery)

      --select <SELECTOR>
          Comma-separated rule or tag selectors to enable (overrides `select` and `ignore` in
          `.omnicoach.toml`)

      --ignore <SELECTOR>
          Comma-separated rule or tag selectors to disable

      --list-rules
          List every rule with its languages and summary, as Markdown

      --tag <LABEL>
          With --list-rules, keep only the rules a `select` label selects (tag, synonym or rule)

      --list-tags
          List the topic tree with each topic's parent, synonyms, description and scope note

      --explain <RULE>
          Print one rule's documentation as Markdown

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

